<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Label colour for a bottom-navigation tab, by state.

    The companion to bottom_nav_item_tint.xml, which does the same job for the icon. They are two
    files rather than one because the selected states differ, and that difference is what the design
    asks for: the active tab's icon sits *inside* the yellow pill and so must be near-black to be
    legible, while its label sits below the pill on the dark bar and so is the yellow itself. Sharing
    one selector would force one of the two to be wrong.

    The unselected colour is shared, so the three inactive tabs read as a single quiet group.

    See bottom_nav_item_tint.xml for why these are fixed colours rather than theme attributes, and
    why the selected state has to be listed first.
-->
<selector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <item
        android:color="@color/nav_item_selected_label"
        android:state_checked="true" />

    <item android:color="@color/nav_item_unselected" />

</selector>
